  "scope": "Classic v11 floating tool preferences and canvas integration; Studio and historical chrome retain their layouts. Eight headless egui GPU frames cover light/dark workspace, brush, View menu and Settings. Native light/dark macOS desktop startup uses isolated settings/recovery and 30 frames each; no OS input/pen/IME or original-app pixel parity claim. Requested desktop size is 1360x900.",
  "regressions_exercised": [
    "Real pointer drags on size/opacity never paint or publish document/history changes, including multipass UI.",
    "Per-stroke size/opacity, release equality, undo/redo, eraser ground and every historical variant remain covered.",
    "A 1024 px numeric brush size retains its value and canvas position; panels clear the fitted canvas and fit 1100x500 windows.",
    "Small canvases remain centered at 1x/2x display scale; fixed clearance avoids brush/eraser canvas shifts.",
    "Zoom pixel mapping starts from a fitted document-centered view; ruler tests verify scroll displacement relative to the stable inset and preserve the resulting origin."
  ],
  "development_evidence": "Initial GUI geometry regressions and temporary diagnostic compile/runtime logs remain alongside successful final checks. GUI full-suite and strict Clippy were repeated after the final numeric/slider changes; preview and native startup are separate executed checks."
